---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BlogPost from '../../components/BlogPost.astro';
import { countries, getReferralUrl } from '../../data/countries';
import { posts } from '../../data/posts';

const country = countries.find((c) => c.slug === 'uk')!;
const referralUrl = getReferralUrl(country);
const post = posts.find((p) => p.slug === 'tesla-referral-code-at-tesla-store')!;

const articleJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: post.title,
  description: post.description,
  datePublished: post.date,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'UK Tesla Model 3 owner' },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Tesla Referral Code UK',
    url: 'https://teslareferralcode.co/',
  },
  mainEntityOfPage: `https://teslareferralcode.co/blog/${post.slug}/`,
};
---
<Layout
  title={`${post.title} | Tesla Referral Code UK`}
  description={post.description}
  country={country}
  canonical={`https://teslareferralcode.co/blog/${post.slug}/`}
  jsonLd={articleJsonLd}
>
  <BlogPost title={post.title} date={post.date} readTime={post.readTime}>
    <p>
      Most people use a Tesla referral code online, by clicking a link before
      they start configuring their car. But you can also use one in person at a
      UK Tesla store, and the perk is the same: 650 free Supercharging miles on
      a Model 3 or Model Y, or £500 off a Model S or Model X. Here is how to do
      it without losing the benefit.
    </p>

    <h2>Why you might want to order in store</h2>
    <p>
      Plenty of buyers prefer ordering in person. You can sit in the car, run
      the spec past an advisor, ask about delivery times in your area, and get
      the paperwork sorted face to face. None of that is possible online. The
      good news is the referral perk works exactly the same whether you order
      from the Tesla website or from a Tesla store.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 1: have the code ready before you go</h2>
    <p>
      Save the code somewhere you can pull it up quickly. The format is a name
      followed by six digits, similar to "hersh671564". The code on the
      <a href="/">main page</a> of this site works for UK orders. Take a
      screenshot or write it down. Do not rely on having signal in the
      showroom, some of them have notoriously bad reception inside.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 2: tell the advisor before they start the order</h2>
    <p>
      Tesla advisors will not ask you for a referral code unprompted. You need
      to bring it up. The right moment is when they sit down at their tablet to
      start filling in your order. Say something like:
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      "Before you submit, I have a referral code I would like to use."
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      Read out the code clearly, or hand them your phone to copy it directly.
      They will type it into the order form in the same field used for online
      referrals. You will see the perk appear in the order summary they pull up
      on screen.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 3: verify the perk on the summary</h2>
    <p>
      Before you sign anything, ask the advisor to show you the order summary.
      For Model S or Model X, there should be a line item showing £500 off
      with the referral code listed next to it. For Model 3 or Model Y, the
      summary will note that 650 free Supercharging miles will be credited to
      your Tesla account after delivery. If you cannot see one of those
      confirmations, do not sign yet. Ask the advisor to add the code or check
      with their manager.
    </p>

    <h2>If the advisor says they cannot add a code</h2>
    <p>
      This is rare, but it happens. Some advisors are new, some are dealing
      with system issues, and some incorrectly believe the code is only valid
      online. If you hit this:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Ask if there is a more senior advisor on the floor who can help.</li>
      <li>If still no luck, ask them to hold off submitting the order for an hour or two.</li>
      <li>Step outside, place the order yourself on tesla.com using the referral link.</li>
      <li>Come back and confirm delivery and trade-in details in person if needed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The order itself is identical either way. The advisor can still help you
      with paperwork, finance, and trade-in after the online order is placed.
    </p>

    <h2>Common questions about in-store referrals</h2>

    <h3>Will the advisor try to talk me out of using a code?</h3>
    <p>
      No. UK Tesla advisors are paid salary, not commission, and the price you
      pay is the same to Tesla whether you used a referral or not. The perk
      comes out of Tesla's marketing budget, not the advisor's sales numbers.
      They will type the code in if you ask.
    </p>

    <h3>Can I add a referral code to an order I placed yesterday?</h3>
    <p>
      Unfortunately, no. Tesla cannot retro-fit a referral code to an existing
      order. If you have already submitted the order without a code, the perk
      is gone for that purchase. The only option is to cancel the order, which
      forfeits your deposit, and place a new one with the code. For most people
      that is not worth it.
    </p>

    <h3>Does the code work on a demo or display car?</h3>
    <p>
      Yes, demo and inventory cars qualify for the referral perk in the UK, as
      long as they are being sold as new. Used Teslas through Tesla's
      approved-used programme do not qualify.
    </p>

    <h2>Ready to order?</h2>
    <p>
      Whether you order online or in person, the referral link is the same. Use
      it before you place the order and the benefit applies automatically.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href={referralUrl} rel="nofollow" class="inline-block mt-2">
        <span class="btn-primary">Use the referral link</span>
      </a>
    </p>

    <h2>Read next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/blog/how-tesla-referral-programme-works-uk/">How the Tesla referral programme works in the UK</a></li>
      <li><a href="/blog/650-free-supercharging-miles-value/">What can you do with 650 free Supercharging miles?</a></li>
      <li><a href="/">Back to the main page and FAQ</a></li>
    </ul>
  </BlogPost>
</Layout>
